Yes. I would refactor it now rather than keep adding chart-specific conditions inside CommonChart.

The cleaner architecture is:

CommonChart should know nothing about MC, Hist, FS Type, CVaR, etc. It should only receive a tooltip configuration describing how series should be displayed. A separate generic utility builds the tooltip.

This also solves your future case where another stacked chart should not strip MC/Hist.

I suggest these 3 files:

CommonChart/
├── CommonChart.tsx
├── CommonChart.css
└── commonChartTooltip.ts

You will add one optional prop:

tooltipConfig={...}

If you don’t send it, the chart can use the normal Highcharts tooltip.

