7. Future stacked chart with completely different requirements

This is the main reason I prefer this design.

Suppose later you have:

Actual EQDL
Limit EQDL
Forecast EQDL
Actual FXVG
Limit FXVG
Forecast FXVG

You don’t touch CommonChart.tsx or commonChartTooltip.ts.

Just configure:

tooltipConfig={{
  mode: 'table',
  categoryLabel: 'Risk Type',
  columns: [
    {
      key: 'actual',
      label: 'Actual',
      seriesPrefix: 'Actual ',
    },
    {
      key: 'limit',
      label: 'Limit',
      seriesPrefix: 'Limit ',
    },
    {
      key: 'forecast',
      label: 'Forecast',
      seriesPrefix: 'Forecast ',
    },
  ],
  removeSeriesPrefixes: [
    'Actual ',
    'Limit ',
    'Forecast ',
  ],
  valueDecimals: 2,
}}

And if another chart should keep its complete series names, simply don’t send:

removeSeriesPrefixes

That’s the key architectural improvement: CommonChart renders the tooltip; the caller describes its structure. You won’t need to keep adding if MC, if Hist, if CVaR, if line chart, etc. to your shared component.
